{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_p1_finding_p1_finding", "label": "P1: what the corridor is an instrument of", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_p1_finding_p1_py", "label": "p1.py (the corridor computation)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_p1_finding_ordering_functional", "label": "One-parameter ordering functional nu = A(n,l) - a*B(n,l)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each step becomes one linear inequality in a, hence one interval; varying B over many candidate forms on the SAME observed order is a test that can fail - invariance would mean the corridor measures the atom, movement that it measures the form."}, {"id": "recovered_p1_finding_concavity_in_node_count", "label": "Strict concavity in the node count p = n - l - 1", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The boundary is exactly beta = 1 across p^beta, ln(1+p), 1-e^-p, atan(p), p/(1+p): every beta<1 is feasible at all 106 steps and every beta>=1 is refuted at 6, so strict concavity is NECESSARY and belongs to the world, while the stabbing points are nu's coordinates and belong to the form."}, {"id": "recovered_p1_finding_piercing_number_three", "label": "The piercing number is 3, invariantly (clique 3)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_p1_finding_the_six_steps", "label": "The six refuting steps (La, Gd, Ac, Th, Cm, Lr)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two unrelated computations return one set of six: the bands whose disjointness forces clique 3 are the same steps that force concavity, and they are the named anomalies - so the exceptions are not noise around the rule, they are the entire measurement, which meets Schwarz's objection on its own terms."}, {"id": "recovered_p1_finding_lowdin_challenge_stands", "label": "Lowdin's challenge still stands", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Concavity in the node count is a necessary condition on the form established by refutation, not a mechanism producing an order from the Schrodinger equation; what is closed is the account of what the instrument measures."}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_p1_finding_p1_finding", "target": "recovered_p1_finding_p1_py", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_p1_finding_p1_finding", "target": "recovered_p1_finding_ordering_functional", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_p1_finding_ordering_functional", "target": "recovered_p1_finding_concavity_in_node_count", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/P1-FINDING.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_p1_finding_p1_finding", "target": "recovered_p1_finding_piercing_number_three", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACT